The MIT grant above covers the shared overlay runtime in this folder written by
the Clear to Air authors (core.js, render.js, the token and skeleton CSS, the
dev server and preview pages), so that overlay packs, which load it at runtime,
stand entirely under MIT. The rest of Clear to Air (agent, control room, relay,
tools) is licensed under the GNU AGPL v3 or later (see LICENSE at the
repository root).

It does NOT cover:

  * the fonts in fonts/. Each keeps its own SIL Open Font License 1.1; the
    full text with its copyright line is next to it as fonts/<Font>-OFL.txt.

  * the name "Clear to Air", the lamp mark or the wordmark. These are
    trademarks and are not licensed under MIT or the AGPL. See TRADEMARKS.md.
